-- title:
--   p-saturation of the integral two-cusp lattice
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a positive integer $M$ with $p \mid M$ but $p^2 \nmid M$, and let $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$ be a subgroup containing every unit whose image under the reduction map $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times} \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^{\times}$ is trivial. Write $\Gamma_H(M)$ for the subgroup [`CohCarrier.GammaH M H`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$, namely the preimage in $\Gamma_0(M)$ of $H$ under the homomorphism sending $\gamma$ to the class of its lower-right entry modulo $M$. For $A$ a subring of $\mathbb{C}$, let $S_A$ denote the set of weight-two cusp forms $f$ on $\Gamma_H(M)$ such that for every $t$ in the Hecke ring `heckeRingH M H 2` (the subring generated by the Hecke generators), every Atkin–Lehner datum $W$ for $(M,p)$ — a factorisation $M = pR$ together with integers $a,b$ satisfying $pa - Rb = 1$ — and every $n$, the $n$-th $q$-expansion coefficients of $t f$ and of $(t f) \mid_2 W$ both lie in $A$; and let $\Lambda_A$ be the $A$-submodule spanned by $S_A$. Let $z$ be a weight-two cusp form on $\Gamma_H(M)$ lying in $S_{\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}}$, where $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ is the image in $\mathbb{C}$ of the subring of rationals whose denominator is coprime to $p$. The assertion is that if $p^{a} z \in \Lambda_{\mathbb{Z}}$ for some natural number $a$, with $\mathbb{Z} \subseteq \mathbb{C}$ the bottom subring, then $z \in \Lambda_{\mathbb{Z}}$.
--
--   This is the $p$-saturation statement comparing the $\mathbb{Z}$-lattice of two-cusp integral weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_H(M)$ with its $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$-integral counterpart: a form that is $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$-integral in the Hecke- and Atkin–Lehner-stable sense and becomes integral after multiplication by a power of $p$ is already in the integral lattice. It is used in the construction of an integral form with prescribed Hecke eigenvalues and prescribed Atkin–Lehner-slashed coefficients, via [`CuspForm.exists_mem_twoCuspLattice_eq_smul_of_forall_qCoeff_eq_mul_of_forall_qCoeff_alSlash_eq_mul`](thm.html#CuspForm.exists_mem_twoCuspLattice_eq_smul_of_forall_qCoeff_eq_mul_of_forall_qCoeff_alSlash_eq_mul), and relies on the fact that under the hypothesis on $H$ the Atkin–Lehner operator at $p$ carries cusp forms on $\Gamma_H(M)$ to cusp forms on $\Gamma_H(M)$.
